statements of financial position | F-6\". So page F-6? But page needs to be an integer minimum 1. F-6 is not an integer. Hmm.\n\nThe document doesn't have explicit page markers in the extracted view for the balance sheet. The table of contents says the consolidated statements of financial position is at F-6. But I can't use \"F-6\" as an integer page.\n\nAlternatively, I can use html_anchor. Is there an anchor? The document contains `<LINK:#fin101275_2>Consolidated statements of financial position` in the index. So the anchor for the balance sheet would be \"fin101275_2\". That's an HTML anchor in the document (id=\"fin101275_2\" presumably). I can use that as html_anchor.\n\nActually, the anchor \"fin101275_2\" is referenced as a link target `<LINK:#fin101275_2>`, which implies there's an element with that id/anchor where the Consolidated statements of financial position begins. So html_anchor: \"fin101275_2\" is reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, I could give page as null? No - the anyOf requires either html_anchor with minLength 1 or page as integer ≥1. Setting page to null wouldn't satisfy. So use html_anchor \"fin101275_2\".\n\nWait, also there's the summary table in Item 5 (T:A:385) \"Consolidated Statements of Financial Position Data\" which shows Total assets 7,193.1 in millions of U.S.$. But the requested field is \"Total assets explicitly reported on the consolidated primary balance sheet\" - the primary balance sheet is the audited consolidated statement of financial position at F-6 (table T:A:638). The value there is 7,193,091 thousand USD.\n\nSo:\n- value: \"7193091\"\n- scale: \"1000\" (in thousands)\n- unit: \"USD\"\n- currency: \"USD\"\n- period: {kind: \"instant\", start: null, end: \"2025-12-31\"}\n- accounting_basis: \"IFRS\"\n- consolidation_scope: \"consolidated\"\n- source_label: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (audited), Item 18\"\n- evidence_quote: Need a quote from the document. The row: `<S:A:C638.24.1>Total assets  |  |  |  |  |  | <S:A:C638.24.7>$  | <S:A:C638.24.8>...7,193,091 ...`. The evidence quote should be plain text like \"Total assets ... $ 7,193,091\". Let me construct: \"Total assets: $7,193,091 (2025 column, in thousands of US dollars)\".\n\nThe evidence_quote has maxLength 400, minLength 1. I'll use: \"Total assets — $ 7,193,091 (Consolidated statements of financial position, 2025 column, in thousands of US dollars)\".\n\n- location:\n  - accession: \"0001193125-26-197494\"\n  - document: \"d101275d20f.htm\"\n  - document_sha256: \"b842756f7ce62b0ae1bd2cf14d6fc3373c61297c0a74934f020493332415326e\"\n  - table: \"Consolidated statements of financial position\"\n  - row: \"Total assets\"\n  - column: \"2025\"\n  - html_anchor: \"fin101275_2\"\n  - page: null (allowed since html_anchor provided; but \"page\" type is [\"integer\", \"null\"], and required fields are accession, document, document_sha256, table, row, column. The anyOf requires html_anchor present. I can include page: null or omit it. Since additionalProperties is false but page is in properties, I can include it or not. I'll include html_anchor only, or html_anchor with page null. Let me include html_anchor: \"fin101275_2\" and page: null. Actually, to be safe, include both: html_anchor: \"fin101275_2\", page: null.\n\n- requested_field: \"Assets\"\n\nAlso note scale: the value is in thousands, so scale \"1000\". Value \"7193091\" means 7,193,091 thousand = 7,193,091,000 dollars.\n\nDouble-check the tagged value: `<S:A:C638.24.8><S:A:A:ixv-64823;n=ifrs-full:Assets;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3>7,193,091` — yes, ifrs-full:Assets for context PAsOn12_31_2025 = 7,193,091 (thousands USD).\n\nThe result should be a single \"found\" result.\n\nOutput JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"statement_candidate_v1\",\n  \"request_id\": \"pilot-aero-summary-neighbour-v1\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"requested_field\": \"Assets\",\n      \"outcome\": \"found\",\n      \"value\": \"7193091\",\n      \"scale\": \"100